Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:31:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] feat(outbox): look up a single event by id

Outbox.get returns an event in any state, or None when it does not exist
(or was published and purged). Audit records carry the id of the event
written with them, so operators and tests can follow that link.

The audit test in test_auth paired audit records with pending events by
position; the controller writes a status event for the new service when
its poll runs between the create and the delete request, which made the
pairing fail. It now looks up each record's event by id.
---
 .../src/forgemesh/controlplane/outbox.py          |  5 +++++
 tests/unit/controlplane/test_auth.py              |  6 +++---
 tests/unit/controlplane/test_outbox.py            | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/control-plane/src/forgemesh/controlplane/outbox.py b/packages/control-plane/src/forgemesh/controlplane/outbox.py
index 3f037a7..952e65c 100644
--- a/packages/control-plane/src/forgemesh/controlplane/outbox.py
+++ b/packages/control-plane/src/forgemesh/controlplane/outbox.py
@@ -239,6 +239,11 @@ class Outbox:
             ),
         )
 
+    def get(self, event_id: str) -> OutboxEvent | None:
+        """按 ``event_id`` 获取任意状态的事件；不存在（或已发布并被清理）时返回 None。"""
+        rows = self._query("SELECT * FROM outbox_events WHERE event_id = ?", (event_id,))
+        return self._row_to_event(rows[0]) if rows else None
+
     def get_pending(self, limit: int = 100) -> list[OutboxEvent]:
